  "body": "Continues #4. The previous diagnostic located 37\u201339 CPU seconds in archive validation but did not separate the work inside it. This adds a temporary three-level observer and a saved-data report for context construction, sampled-state decoding/scoring, full-checkpoint decoding and prior full-control verification. Defining scientific functions and all 444 previous scientific files remain unchanged.\n\n[Report and full inclusive/residual table](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/805b3ea/docs/parent-archive-cpu.md#what-the-complete-comparison-found--november-17):\n\n| Instrumented cost read | Before reference | After reference |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Archive root, parent CPU seconds | 36.482965 | 36.735498 |\n| Combined sampled/full/prior checkpoint decoding | 16.292417 | 15.881237 |\n| Two explicit materialized context builds | 8.883226 | 8.748734 |\n| Sampled-state scoring | 3.014329 | 3.072910 |\n\nDecoding includes validation and full-checkpoint metric recomputation. Inclusive parents already contain children; the report and figure stack disjoint leaf CPU and parent residuals. Prior-full residual is not a pure context/hashing measurement. Complete ordinary/profiled commands take **394.975386 / 398.778299 seconds**; enclosing CLI **797.198346 / 1,800**. One ordered pair does not establish stable overhead, a causal speedup, production costs or playing strength.\n\nAll original three reads, 432 profiles, 1,152 conditions and three comparison-only workers remain. All 802 selected calls have exact declared parents/order and full restoration. Complete scalar/calculated-replay identity matches both arms and the previous published result exactly; maximum independent scalar discrepancy **1.8474111129762605e-13 chips < 1e-9**. No optimizer or new training was introduced.\n\nThe [prospective plan](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/1a6c9d7/docs/parent-archive-cpu.md) preceded source and outcomes. [All six source roles and ten tested tools](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/1f69894/results/parent-archive-cpu/checks.json) qualified `a9c672a`: bases **5,220 / 69 skipped / 150 deselected each**, optional **2,127 each**, both hosted bases pass with actual patch/NumPy/all uv and whole-tree checks. The initial hosted 3.11 job hit the unchanged 25-minute limit at 88%; its full log/annotation remain. Only that unchanged-source software job was retried; carried 3.12 retains its original execution identity.\n\n[Own proof](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/bc5a3dd/results/parent-archive-cpu/software-raw-manifest.json) was public and actually verified before reference work; [all 27 raw pair files](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/blob/a9097f4/results/parent-archive-cpu/pair-raw-manifest.json) were public and verified before analysis. Own proof: complete **6.639983 / 180 seconds**, actual saved software replay identical, two explicitly synthetic 401-call trees. These fixtures do not establish real cost-loader coverage or new independent poker math.\n\nAll three numerical exports reproduce byte for byte on actual **3.11.17 / NumPy 2.4.6** and **3.12.15 / NumPy 2.5.4**, with **73 numerical entry points blocked**, zero forbidden calls and raw unchanged. Both figures visually inspected. OpenSpiel 2.0.2 / Apache-2.0 stays scalar comparison-only; installed license read/pinned before fresh use. The learning journal and work log explain the result and next question: verify identical repeated context inputs/results and safe reuse before proposing a cache.\n\n**Final qualification passes all six roles** on complete report revision `805b3eaf27398ede2293e1347c2a50db5760d17f`, unchanged scientific fingerprint `3c343e8f8963a4d73e0ea6a277db13d57f06918ba45cb1d5216be151e7089e5d` (447 files):\n\n| Runtime | Final local base | Relevant optional | Actual hosted execution |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 3.11.17 / NumPy 2.4.6 | 5,220 / 69 skipped / 150 deselected; 722.13s | 2,127; 416.99s | 5,220; 1005.47s, attempt 3 |\n| 3.12.15 / NumPy 2.5.4 | 5,220 / 69 skipped / 150 deselected; 695.43s | 2,127; 356.06s | 5,220; 1053.37s, actual attempt 2 |\n\n[Final hosted run](https://github.com/jimmy-sim/poker-ai/actions/runs/44080893080) confirms actual patch/NumPy, every uv choice and entire checkout `ec6020dbb5f5bb89e460111872b0b6b2b5235e29`, tree `2baa5a19de2bd288fc994320b1cbc6dedb8b41e8` equal to the PR head. Carried 3.12 keeps actual job `134045623062` / attempt 2; it is not a new execution. Both hosted bases retain the existing historical rounding warning. Local lint, formatting, strict typing (816 files) and hooks pass. Documentation checks pass 529 local destinations, 10 images, affected anchors, balanced fences and preserved markers.\n\nAll hosted cancellations and official 25-minute-limit annotations remain. Initial final jobs stopped at 84% / 88%; the second 3.11 job stopped at 83%. Only incomplete software roles were retried, with source, all checks and limits unchanged; no scientific pair was rerun. Earlier progress timestamps show broad 1.42\u20131.54\u00d7 wall slowdowns. An initial association with image versions is **not a cause**: the later successful 3.11 job also used image `20261111.370.1`. This counterexample is retained with the initial observations; hardware/image performance is not isolated by these logs.\n\nClosing PR #84 receipts and protected-main verification are retained in this PR's initial documentation batch. A fresh read-only snapshot confirms all ten original uncommitted result bytes/statuses unchanged. Guarded history merge and actual-main preservation/data checks follow these verified final roles.\n\nSelf-review focuses on unchanged caller behavior, exact nested clock accounting, failure retention, publication ordering and source/runtime provenance. Codex-assisted implementation, execution and documentation; no independent code reviewer or human hours implied. The **912.54/900-second forecast** and **2.390%/1% accuracy** failures remain. No stronger/default/fresh/global admission or competitive full-game strength claim.\n",
